# The agent's home (typed), as the agent case's board: virtio-blk and fs
# give the disk's data volume, which holds the home; virtio-net and inet
# the network; agentd starts after them, and makes the home's parts,
# its constitution from agent/CONSTITUTION.md. On the host, e2e.sh runs
# tools/api-proxy/e2e_serve.py (serve): the stand-in, answering from
# script.json and checking each request as checks.json says, and the
# proxy in front of it on @PORT@, which keeps the home's backup in
# build/e2e/agent_home.backup. In a first run agent the script writes
# the rules anew and a memory and its index, and tries the constitution,
# which is refused; a second's turn goes on the same conversation, the
# first's words in its messages, and its system prompt, made anew,
# holds the new rules and index. Then the history is listed and undone,
# the home backed up, the conversation with it, a file changed behind
# the history's back, and the backup restored.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/uart noecho
start /sbin/virtio-blk
start /sbin/fs
start /sbin/virtio-net
start /sbin/inet
start /sbin/agentd
dev /sbin/uart
dev /sbin/virtio-blk
dev /sbin/virtio-net
